  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<div align=\"center\">\n  <img width=\"140\" src=\"./assets/icon-full.webp\" alt=\"dsh-workflow-lite 图标\"><br>\n  <img width=\"360\" src=\"./assets/wordmark.png\" alt=\"dsh-workflow-lite\">\n</div>\n\n<div align=\"center\">\n\n简体中文 | [English](./README.en.md)\n\n</div>\n\n<div align=\"center\">\n\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@xiaoso/dsh-workflow-lite)\n[](./LICENSE)\n[](https://nodejs.org)\n[](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness)\n[](https://xiaoso456.github.io/dsh-workflow-lite/)\n\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "[DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) 的软工作流插件，基于提示词编排：在画布上设计流程，编译成计划提示词，由模型按计划执行。连线可带**任意条件**，支持顺序、并行、汇合、条件分支、循环、回退等流程结构，无需额外的执行引擎。\n\n> **实验阶段**：功能和数据格式仍在调整，后续任何版本都可能包含不兼容的改动。\n\n**使用文档**：<https://xiaoso456.github.io/dsh-workflow-lite/>——安装、上手、画布展示和各项设置，带截图。\n\n[](./CHANGELOG.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "安装",
      "text": "适配 DeepSeek Harness 0.2.0 与 0.2.1，包括它们的各个预览版（如 0.2.1-rc.2）。"
    },
    {
      "section": "网页版",
      "text": "需要 Node.js 22 及以上。\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add @xiaoso/dsh-workflow-lite\ndsh web\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "桌面端",
      "text": "1. 在侧边栏打开「**插件**」，点击「**添加插件**」→「**安装第三方插件**」。\n2. 填入 `@xiaoso/dsh-workflow-lite`，点击「**安装**」。\n3. 重启 DeepSeek Harness。\n\n安装完成后，会话页顶部会出现「**工作流**」标签页。"
    },
    {
      "section": "让模型创建",
      "text": "在对话中用一句话描述流程，例如：\n\n> 建一个工作流：先写代码，再审查，审查不通过就回去修复，最多三轮。\n\n模型会创建工作流，画布上会同步显示。检查无误后，点击右上角「**执行**」，或让模型直接执行。"
    },
    {
      "section": "手动编辑",
      "text": "1. 打开「工作流」标签页，新建一个工作流。\n2. 从左侧步骤库将步骤拖到画布上，填写提示词并连线。\n3. 点击右上角「**执行**」，或在对话中请模型执行该工作流。"
    },
    {
      "section": "跟踪进度",
      "text": "在「工作流设置」中开启「**记录运行状态**」，此后每次执行都会生成一条记录，画布随进度更新。执行记录、工作流与版本统一在画布左上角的「**工作流中心**」中管理。"
    },
    {
      "section": "功能",
      "text": "| 功能 | 说明 |\n|---|---|\n| 画布编辑 | 拖拽步骤与连线，支持「通过 / 不通过」分支和循环，一键整理布局 |\n| 资源 | 为步骤指定要读写的文件、文件夹、网址或 Skill |\n| 执行前提问 | 执行前向用户收集必要信息，答案随计划交给模型 |\n| 模型协作编辑 | 模型可以直接创建、修改工作流，画布实时同步 |\n| 运行状态 | 执行进度实时显示在画布上；可查看每一步的摘要、调整状态并通知模型 |\n| 画布展示（实验性） | 看板、图片、文档、日志、表格和文件夹直接显示在画布上，执行时自动更新；循环每一轮的产出可以回看、对比 |\n| 文件预览 | 实例里的资源点开就能看：Markdown、HTML 页面（可做成每轮更新的看板，随时查看循环产出）、图片；文件夹分左右两栏浏览 |\n| 版本管理 | 保存版本、添加说明、对比差异、随时切换 |\n| 导入导出 | 把工作流和选中的版本打成一个 `.wflite.zip`，可以连同用到的文件与 Skill 一起打包；导入前列出每样东西放到哪 |\n| 导出成 Skill | 把一个版本编译成 skill（SKILL.md + 每步的任务描述 + 打包的文件与 Skill），不装插件也能用；下载 zip，或直接装到本机的 `~/.agents/skills` |\n| 记忆（实验性） | 工作流把跑通的做法和踩过的坑记成 skill，下次执行照着走；可以在「记忆」页管理、存版本，随工作流包导出 |\n| 工作流中心 | 集中管理各会话的执行记录、全部工作流与版本，以及插件设置 |\n| 界面 | 浅色、深色各四套配色主题，跟随 DSH 自动切换；中文 / English |"
    },
    {
      "section": "路径变量",
      "text": "资源里的路径和产出根目录可以写下面两个变量，执行时换成实际的位置：\n\n| 变量 | 写在哪 | 换成什么 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `{workflow}` | 资源里的文件、文件夹路径，如 `{workflow}/refs/notes.md` | 这个工作流自己的目录（默认 `~/.dsh/workflow-lite/assets/<工作流名>/`）。在哪个工作区执行都读写同一份，工作流改名、导出时一起带走 |\n| `{instance}` | 「工作流设置」里的「产出根目录」，如默认值 `.workflow-lite/runs/{instance}/out` | 这次执行的实例 id，每次执行的产出各放一处 |\n\n旧版本写的 `{assets}/…` 照样能用，打开工作流时会自动改成 `{workflow}/…`。"
    },
    {
      "section": "实验性功能",
      "text": "下面的功能还在试验，行为和数据格式后续可能调整；除了工作流记忆，还有上面功能表里的「画布展示」。"
    },
    {
      "section": "工作流记忆",
      "text": "让工作流把跑通的做法记下来，下次执行照着走，目的是加快复杂工作流的执行。\n\n- **使用**：给步骤开一份，或从步骤库「基础」里把「记忆」拖到画布上，作为整个工作流共用的一份；加的时候选已有的，或新建。\n- **内容**：一条记忆是一个 skill 文件夹，开头的「快速路径」是下次最省事的走法。各步骤把经验写在回复里，工作流结束时由模型整理进去。\n- **管理**：在工作流中心的「记忆」页查看、存版本；导出时可选带不带。\n- **限制**：多个实例同时改同一条记忆不加锁，后写的覆盖先写的；重新导出并覆盖安装 Skill，会覆盖已装 skill 里攒下的记忆。\n\n记忆只是一个快捷配置。需要更复杂的玩法时，建议自己用「资源」加提示词实现。\n\n**效果还在验证，欢迎反馈。** 早期在同一个工作流上重复执行的试验里没有看到稳定的提速，后来加入了「快速路径」，是否有用需要更多真实的工作流来检验。"
    },
    {
      "section": "工作原理",
      "text": "1. **设计**：在画布上编排步骤，为每一步写好交给执行者的提示词，用分支和循环描述流程。\n2. **编译**：插件把工作流整理成一份计划提示词，写明执行顺序、循环条件、每一步的输入与产出。\n3. **执行**：模型按计划自行安排执行方式（直接完成、派发子代理或组建团队），并把进度同步回画布。\n\n插件本身不包含执行引擎，也无需额外服务；调度与判断交由当前会话中的模型完成。"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[MIT](./LICENSE) © xiaoso"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<div align=\"center\">\n  <img width=\"140\" src=\"./assets/icon-full.webp\" alt=\"dsh-workflow-lite icon\"><br>\n  <img width=\"360\" src=\"./assets/wordmark.png\" alt=\"dsh-workflow-lite\">\n</div>\n\n<div align=\"center\">\n\n[简体中文](./README.md) | English\n\n</div>\n\n<div align=\"center\">\n\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@xiaoso/dsh-workflow-lite)\n[](./LICENSE)\n[](https://nodejs.org)\n[](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness)\n[](https://xiaoso456.github.io/dsh-workflow-lite/)\n\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "A soft-workflow plugin for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness), built on prompt orchestration: design a flow on a canvas, compile it into a plan prompt, and let the model carry it out. Edges can carry **any condition**, and flows can be sequential, parallel, joined, conditionally branched, looped or rolled back, with no extra execution engine required.\n\n> **Experimental**: features and data formats are still changing, and any release may include breaking changes."
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "**Documentation**: <https://xiaoso456.github.io/dsh-workflow-lite/> (installation, first steps, canvas display and settings, with screenshots).\n\n[](./CHANGELOG.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Works with DeepSeek Harness 0.2.0 and 0.2.1, including their preview builds (such as 0.2.1-rc.2)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Web",
      "text": "Requires Node.js 22 or later.\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add @xiaoso/dsh-workflow-lite\ndsh web\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Desktop",
      "text": "1. Open **Plugins** in the sidebar, then click **Add plugin** → **Install a third-party plugin**.\n2. Enter `@xiaoso/dsh-workflow-lite` and click **Install**.\n3. Restart DeepSeek Harness.\n\nOnce installed, a **Workflow** tab appears at the top of the session page."
    },
    {
      "section": "Ask the model",
      "text": "Describe the flow in one sentence in the conversation, for example:\n\n> Create a workflow: write the code, then review it; if the review fails, go back and fix it, at most three rounds.\n\nThe model creates the workflow and the canvas shows it as it is built. When it looks right, click **Run** in the top-right corner, or ask the model to run it."
    },
    {
      "section": "Edit by hand",
      "text": "1. Open the **Workflow** tab and create a workflow.\n2. Drag steps from the library on the left onto the canvas, fill in their prompts, and connect them.\n3. Click **Run** in the top-right corner, or ask the model in the conversation to run the workflow."
    },
    {
      "section": "Follow progress",
      "text": "Turn on **Record run state** in **Workflow settings**. Every run then leaves a record and the canvas updates as the model works. Run records, workflows and versions are managed in the **Workflow hub**, opened from the top-left corner of the canvas."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "| Feature | Description |\n|---|---|\n| Canvas editing | Drag steps and connect them, with pass / fail branches and loops; tidy the layout in one click |\n| Resources | Attach files, folders, URLs or Skills that a step reads or writes |\n| Pre-run questions | Collect the information a run needs from the user; answers are passed to the model with the plan |\n| Model co-editing | The model can create and edit workflows directly, and the canvas updates live |\n| Run state | Progress appears on the canvas as it happens; read each step's summary, adjust its state, and the model is notified |\n| Canvas display (beta) | Dashboards, images, documents, logs, tables and folders show right on the canvas and update during a run; review and compare each round of a loop |\n| File preview | Open a run's resources in place: Markdown, HTML pages (make one a dashboard updated every round to follow a loop's output), images; browse folders in a two-pane view |\n| Versions | Save versions with notes, compare differences, switch back at any time |\n| Import / export | Pack a workflow and the versions you pick into one `.wflite.zip`, optionally with the files and Skills it uses; before importing, see where each it"
    },
    {
      "section": "Path variables",
      "text": "Resource paths and the output root accept two variables, replaced with real locations at run time:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Path variables",
      "text": "| Variable | Where | Becomes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `{workflow}` | File and folder paths in resources, e.g. `{workflow}/refs/notes.md` | The workflow's own folder (by default `~/.dsh/workflow-lite/assets/<workflow name>/`). Every workspace reads and writes the same copy, and it moves with the workflow when you rename or export it |\n| `{instance}` | **Output root** in **Workflow settings**, e.g. the default `.workflow-lite/runs/{instance}/out` | The id of this run's instance, so each run keeps its outputs apart |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Path variables",
      "text": "Paths written as `{assets}/…` by earlier versions still work and become `{workflow}/…` when the workflow is opened."
    },
    {
      "section": "Experimental features",
      "text": "These features are still being tried out, and their behavior and data formats may change. Besides workflow memory, there is **Canvas display** in the feature table above."
